{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And I will hear, for I am gracious.</b> Ramban explained: a person might say of that poor man whose garment is pledged — he is unworthy, he is not fit, and I bear no sin from him if I take his cloak and do not return it, for his cry will not be heard by El. Therefore it is written ״כי חנון אני״ — 'for I am gracious' — that is, He grants favor and accepts the supplication of every person even though he is not fit, for חנון is from the root חנם, as they interpreted, may their memory be blessed (Exodus 33:19): ״וחנותי את אשר אחון״ — even though he is not worthy and fit. The meaning is that He hears the cry of all who entreat Him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:05.780164170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}